# Gustav and Elisabeth Durst at their supper table in the dungeon (death_house_dungeon_1). Every road ends in a
# fight (durst_reunion: two ghasts, 900 XP, above High at level 2, as in the book), but what the party learns first, and
# whether the Dursts are shaken by news of their children, changes it.

~ start
Narrator: A man and a woman sit at a laid supper table by the light of one candle, their fine clothes hanging off them. Their fingers are long and grey, and the plates in front of them are not empty.
Gustav [smile]: Guests. Elisabeth, guests. Do sit. We so rarely have anyone down.
Elisabeth [sly]: They came down the children's way. Didn't you, dears.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Two of them, and they've laid the table. I'm sure it's... no. Don't let them get behind us.
if not name:kip_smudgewick
  interject class:fighter: Mind the table. They'll come over it.
endif
-> choose

~ choose
* Who are you? -> who
* What happened to your children? -> children
* Where is Walter? -> walter
* [Intimidation DC 13] Tell us about your cult. Now. -> confess | bristle
* [Persuasion DC 15] You were people once. Tell us the truth while you still can. -> confess | bristle
* [if flag.death_house_children_at_rest] Your children are at rest. They're free of you. -> shaken
* Enough talk. Attack. -> fight

~ who
Gustav: Gustav Durst, and my wife, Elisabeth. This is our house, you understand. All of it. Even the parts that never appeared on the plans.
-> choose

~ children
Elisabeth: Upstairs. Safe. We locked them in so they wouldn't see.
Gustav [sad]: We meant to go back up for them. And then we were so very hungry.
if flag.death_house_children_truth
  interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Your children starved in that room, waiting for you. Hear it. Whatever you are now, hear it.
  if not name:liriel_dawnsong
    interject class:cleric: They waited for you until they died. Remember that, if you can remember anything.
  endif
endif
-> choose

~ walter
Elisabeth [angry]: That one was never mine. He was the first gift. The finest gift we had.
Gustav: And the gift was refused. He wanted nothing from us. Not even that.
if not flag.death_house_learned_walter
  set death_house_learned_walter
  set death_house_lore += 1
endif
interject name:ratatoille: Refused. By "him", I take it. Nobody in this house will say his name.
-> choose

~ confess
Gustav: We wanted what he has. Forever. So we fed the house, and the house fed the thing below, and we waited for him to notice.
Elisabeth [sly]: One must die, so the rest may live forever. We only got the second half wrong.
Gustav [smile]: Go down and see. The altar will ask you too. Everyone gets asked.
if not flag.death_house_dursts_confessed
  set death_house_dursts_confessed
  set death_house_lore += 1
endif
Narrator: Gustav dabs his mouth with a napkin and stands. Supper, it seems, is over.
combat durst_reunion

~ bristle
Gustav [angry]: Manners. In my own house.
Narrator: Elisabeth is already over the table.
combat durst_reunion

~ shaken
Narrator: Elisabeth's fork stops halfway to her mouth. For one moment the hunger leaves both their faces, and what's left is worse: two parents who have just remembered.
Elisabeth [sad]: Rosavalda?
Gustav [sad]: Thornboldt?
Narrator: Then the hunger comes back. But you have the moment, and you use it.
combat durst_reunion_shaken

~ fight
Narrator: Gustav sighs, the way a host sighs at a broken glass.
combat durst_reunion
